### `BufferedReader eats the request body (plain-HTTP proxy)`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| POST/PUT through the proxy fails (origin 400/500, form login loops or redirects) while GETs, CONNECT, and VPN mode all work | Header parsing with `BufferedReader` then relaying the **raw** socket stream: body bytes read ahead into the reader's 8KB buffer are silently dropped | Parse headers byte-exact from a `BufferedInputStream` up to CRLF-CRLF and relay from the **same** stream object. Differential test: plain POST fails while an `Expect: 100-continue` POST (body sent after headers) works |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Keep-alive follow-up misrouted (absolute-form request line)`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| First proxied request fine, same-connection follow-up 404s (classic: auth retry after a 401); fresh connections and VPN mode work | Proxy rewrote the absolute-form request line only for the first request; keep-alive follow-ups reached the origin verbatim (`GET http://host/path HTTP/1.1` — unroutable) | Plain-HTTP proxy must rewrite the request line **per request**: loop over requests, byte-exact header parse, fresh origin connection (`Connection: close`) per request, pump exact `Content-Length`. Do not "fix" by force-closing the client connection — clients pipeline/reuse and those bytes race the teardown ("target server failed to respond") |
| Origin resets before responding (502, empty response) after a GET | `shutdownOutput()` (FIN) sent right after request headers — some servers treat early half-close as client abort | Never FIN the origin socket to signal end-of-request; the request is self-describing (`Connection: close` + `Content-Length`) |

