### `stopProxy stalls after link loss / Doze resume`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| OFF or swap: many `STOP received`, no `stopProxy begin`, `http_proxy` stays `127.0.0.1:*` for 15s+; Doze resume logs `zts_node_start result=0` but never `node UP` for hours | NODE_UP/join waits used blocking native delay **inside** the single-thread libzt dispatcher (`withNode` + `withTimeoutOrNull` — timeout never runs while that thread is blocked). `startStopMutex` held across the wait; STOP queued. `disable()` lived only inside `stopProxy()` behind the mutex | Poll **outside** `withNode` (`pollUntil` + coroutine `delay`). Release mutex before long waits; launch ensure loop without holding it. On STOP: `disableBlocking()` + `isRunning=false` **before** mutex. Orchestrator `applyOff` / `stopProxyStack`: `disable()` before `stopAndAwait`. `stopAndAwait` waits `fullyStopped`, not merely `!isRunning`. Bind HTTP + enable Global **before** NODE_UP (captive portal). Retry NODE_UP miss with stop+backoff+start; join miss re-join only |

