### `get_id is not node up`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| UI node ID `fffffffffffffffe`; join “Node not up” | `zts_node_get_id` returns `ZTS_ERR_SERVICE` (−2) when the service isn’t running; `id != 0` treated as up | Valid id is 40-bit `1..0xffffffffff`. Never publish error-range ids |
| After Doze resume: lifecycle Starting, real identity, no `node UP` log, join hangs ~30s; OFF→PROXY heals | `get_id` can return a real address before the `NODE_UP` event; ensure loop skips restart | Wait for **`NODE_UP` event**, not `get_id` and not `NODE_ONLINE` (ONLINE = roots/moon — airgap). Timeout → `stop()` + backoff. Opt-in storage+handler reinit under Pause-in-Doze (default off) |

